{
 "format": "patchkamer-tunes",
 "formatVersion": 1,
 "version": "1.1.0",
 "device": "nl.patchkamer.loopslicer",
 "name": "Loop Slicer Break Chops",
 "author": "Freek van Gool",
 "license": "CC0-1.0",
 "description": "Re-sequencing patterns for two-bar drum loops cut into 16 equal slices, for jungle, breakbeat and drum and bass: each pattern step plays one slice (an eighth note) at its own length. They assume a loop with the kick on the first beat and the snare on beats 2 and 4, like the Break Loops in the Samples tab; on another loop the slices fall elsewhere. Checked on paper, not listened to. The folder Amen Chops adds ten more re-sequencings for jungle and drum and bass: swapped bars, snare ladders, doubled kicks, rolls, a reversed run, a sixteenth-note cut on 32 slices (needs a two-bar loop) and a half-speed version. Checked on paper, not listened to.",
 "tags": [
